<node id="&quot;RFR LOAN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FACILITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A loan type where interest rate fluctuations are based on the risk-free rate."&lt;SEP&gt;"A loan where the interest rate is determined based on a risk-free rate (RFR)."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of loan that is tied to the RFR and subject to its interest rate adjustments."&lt;SEP&gt;"An RFR Loan is a type of short-term borrowing arrangement that utilizes a reference rate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Another type of structured loan arrangement subject to prepayment by the Borrower under specified conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loans that are based on a Risk-Free Rate rather than traditional benchmarks."&lt;SEP&gt;"denominated in US Dollars and referenced with the Daily Simple SOFR."</data>
