<node id="&quot;DEBTOR RELIEF LAW&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"REGULATORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A body of law governing the procedures available to debtors in financial distress, including bankruptcy procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Debtor Relief Law refers to legal frameworks under which a borrower may seek relief from debt obligations, affecting Lenders' positions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laws that may affect the repayment obligations of the Borrower in situations such as bankruptcy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laws that provide protection for debtors and manage the process in situations of default or bankruptcy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Legal framework referenced in relation to any proceedings that may affect the Borrower's obligations and the Lender's rights under the agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9a3a25d833dc5c9dbf51acf95e17a8c4594980b2f8443c4b8cd76209f44fc05e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b8991cd9ed9ee197640df0ae2da83d3076642e19ac632e7680d69e182501d14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de89031fb05d6268cdaade8e6f8ee037aff51ae412cca50ea016ef150ccff1b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64237ca7ee70ecd83f0946b9540617351d1643eee21284e4825864ab52ed6728&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bc131ae3a964914441757eff595809353daad8779a57973721c7705114343eb</data>
