<node id="&quot;COMPANY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"COMPANY"</data>
  <data key="d1">The entity referred to as "COMPANY" is a legal business entity actively engaged in various transactions, primarily within the context of credit agreements and loan agreements. As the borrower or another relevant party in these agreements, the COMPANY holds rights and obligations tied to the loan transactions, which include prompt payment of all debts and compliance with the terms stipulated in the Loan Documents.

The COMPANY’s role encompasses a range of responsibilities: it is involved in maintaining and managing its financial obligations, including Material Indebtedness, which aggregates to an outstanding principal amount of $1,500,000,000 or more. The entity is also tasked with ensuring compliance with legal requirements concerning taxes, liens, and lease agreements, as well as fulfilling representation duties in the context of ongoing litigation. It must adhere to specific obligations, including managing the relationships with lenders, paying fees and interest, and should a need arise, compensating lenders for costs incurred due to changes in law.

As part of its operations, the COMPANY is responsible for delivering necessary documentation under the Loan Documents and ensuring that its operational practices promote compliance among its directors, officers, and employees. The COMPANY is also involved in credit facilities, is capable of designating additional subsidiaries for loan applications, and has the authority to modify aggregate commitments when necessary.

In relation to security interests, the COMPANY takes ownership of relevant assets and complies with related liabilities. It engages with the Administrative Agent and lenders, participating in the syndication of credit facilities and managing communications regarding funding obligations. The COMPANY is noted for using audited financial statements to reflect its financial condition and results of operations, underscoring its fiscal responsibility.

Additionally, the COMPANY agrees not to assert any claims against the Administrative Agent and recognizes that it is not considered an Affected Financial Institution regarding sanctions. It has the right to replace Non-Extending Lenders with Eligible Assignees and is integral in executing the Existing 364-Day Revolving Credit Agreement and other associated agreements.

Overall, the COMPANY operates in compliance with extensive legal and financial obligations, positioning itself as a critical entity within the agreements that govern its financial transactions and relationships with lenders.</data>
