<node id="&quot;ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"AGENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">The "ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT" is an entity responsible for managing the administrative functions related to loan agreements and financial arrangements on behalf of lenders. This role involves ensuring compliance with the terms and conditions of these agreements and facilitating communication between borrowers and lenders. Specifically, the Administrative Agent oversees various tasks including notifying lenders and borrowers of important loan details, managing payment processes, coordinating the administration of loans, and handling responsibilities such as determining interest rates, processing tax documentation, and executing amendments or waivers.

In practice, the Administrative Agent is typically a financial institution, such as CITIBANK, N.A. or Bank of America, N.A., designated to fulfill these obligations as outlined in the loan documents. The agent also manages the operational aspects related to the loans, including maintaining compliance with credit terms and handling any issues that arise, such as defaults.

Moreover, the Administrative Agent is tasked with collecting regulatory information, ensuring the distribution of payments among lenders and borrowers, and maintaining accurate records of all transactions. They play a crucial role in determining benchmark replacements, notifying parties about any significant changes, and representing the lenders in various administrative capacities.

The Administrative Agent must act responsibly and in accordance with fiduciary standards, benefiting from the representations and warranties made by lenders. Their authority includes the management of loan arrangements, responses to lender determinations, and overseeing the execution of prepayments as needed. Overall, this entity is vital in orchestrating the complex interactions within the lending framework, ensuring that all parties adhere to agreed-upon terms while facilitating smooth financial operations.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-58c0bae8fcfd224975631aaaec56da60866e29fb6d48da0c39451feabf425c1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40560da6e1561d9b7bbc87da2fb1251546ce2526102f0f961d2c1a4ce09d2d3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85ef6ac5a1c6b87ea330f630646059e0bb68c988df4982313a1ca1446ecc64c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-928a1ae0961152b09f4da25a11b845d54b0eee3632984d5b436203de958c27f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c26e344604cf7726d7004ea668272ac6ce202e8a6390a06a6db514777f3cf2f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b8991cd9ed9ee197640df0ae2da83d3076642e19ac632e7680d69e182501d14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de89031fb05d6268cdaade8e6f8ee037aff51ae412cca50ea016ef150ccff1b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e8504ff4ba8ed9fb6b7bfc804b36759673b68ac8657e9e296cd54aa36268736&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a62e841067104d99b0735c0f8420451b33972e5ad9ef2f9bbc84a3a7a7f3ed5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bab89d27ef551b922b5169dcbc7ae230a9d03b5122a39dbe55e516b636b5fa1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ff5e2434da655a2671e0dad2380df7ed33831a7ffce6ba8ccd31c237a80d8f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5837b4e906ab93df88dde035c5e968021e4b88da4155614ac6fd5c04dd10bb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae141e7df14e0e4a6e6cc20f2d0ae5a460cfdb6b5bada2b428f3a3fa46ab9962&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e5aa2c03b189bfa8ef483975b0359e291d82a6beb7efd71f9e1fbd8af45fe4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1802684c18fb32d6b6b57dfc8ae152b1f62a6d7e7db1fb9e15d0b2ec9c21a9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6103744a90662e90d48bd1542329aabc2055c94174e6974793f86b7f123c9861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-040bab39da9786ff0f3cafd4425e251c09564b0124c1823abcad4bb4a496cb18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1841685683abf32e2cb2a9878e3ab222d164d7a7b0358caf1fdac82f1c2a6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f8c4736ec9a956967fd71cc423e20057296a32f721a9c65287373540618cfd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f50b17bab75f31965c93c4d7bd2f14b658481cc3c8810926c4014b58d70bda0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42d0ef1a853dfae1ebeda59d8a271d919e3401384ff07dde2d60832a2bc531d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10e954958658426a2f999194f3230158be979bc90b4cc12f53af4155628dfb6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e1225c5fdbc1f1d590f8bc86c6948259008fff171a6edcd23aa01eb1514e7f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2997033e9e9586a5d8ae522596b79da333d35edef15546a52e86c722b6d5025e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-671f3b38bd6c6bb7fc6cb71e54f93c174