<edge source="&quot;LENDER&quot;" target="&quot;ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">275.0</data>
  <data key="d5">The relationship between the ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT and the LENDER encompasses a structured collaboration where the LENDER provides funds while the ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT manages and coordinates those funds to ensure smooth transactions among all parties involved. The ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT acts on behalf of the LENDER, possessing the same rights and powers as any other LENDER, which includes managing and facilitating various administrative functions related to the loan agreement.

The ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT is responsible for a range of activities, including maintaining records of loans made by each LENDER to the Borrowers, executing transactions on behalf of the LENDERS, and managing communications and materials between the COMPANY and the LENDERS. They are also tasked with ensuring compliance with the USA PATRIOT Act and may incur expenses on behalf of the LENDER to enforce rights and protect interests.

The LENDER must communicate necessary information to the ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT, including documentation requested by the COMPANY and any notifications regarding Material Non-Public Information (MNPI) for procedural compliance. In the event of a loan default, the ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT has the authority to declare the LENDER's commitment terminated and works with the LENDER to manage liabilities and compensation.

Both parties engage actively in the management of loan-related matters; the LENDER confers rights and obligations to the ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT under the agreement and relies on their expertise for administrative tasks, ensuring adherence to the terms outlined in the loan documents. The relationship is further defined by clear communication protocols, where the ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT informs the LENDER of significant matters, such as funding and compliance requirements, while the LENDER must notify the ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT when required to assign rights under the agreement.

Notably, the ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT does not act as a fiduciary concerning the assets of the LENDER under this agreement, emphasizing the cooperative yet independent roles they play in the management of loan transactions and compliance obligations.</data>
